{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChGzrKUsaLEvGKkyepHLK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This isn't a bug, so I haven't written a repro script.\n\nClocks in America/Toronto go back one hour at 02:00 on Sunday 1 November 2026, so the night of Saturday 31 October has an extra hour. Going to bed at 23:00 and getting up at 07:00 gives 9 hours of real elapsed time, even though the wall clock shows an 8-hour gap. Between 01:00 and 02:00 the clock reads that hour twice.\n\n`Night.duration` in `src/nightjar/models.py:52` converts both times to UTC before subtracting. That is the correct approach, and the repo's notes warn about the opposite mistake. I ran your exact night through it and it returned `9:00:00`.\n\nIf you actually slept 8 hours, the diary's 9 hours is still right as elapsed time. The 8-hour figure comes from subtracting wall-clock times, which ignores the repeated hour.\n\nIf you'd like the UI to flag nights that cross a DST change, say so and I can raise that as a separate improvement. That would be a feature request, not a bug fix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":213,"cache_read_input_tokens":23985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":213},"output_tokens":356,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb92526a-b7b1-456e-b381-9fd8166a4886","uuid":"9939544a-80be-41a9-97d9-c1c471f19ce3","timestamp":"2026-11-22T00:11:56.479Z","request_id":"req_011ChGzrKHDn6P12n6qffXFd"}
